  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Cursed Transmutation — Innate Technique (3rd level)</em></p><p>At 3rd level, you have studied the structure of your technique and learned greater ways to utilize it:</p>\n<p><strong>Transmute Explosion</strong>. On a hit with a weapon attack, you can spend 2 cursed energy to transmute the attack and force the creature to make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d6 fire damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful save. This increases to 3d6 at 6th level, 4d6 at 11th level and 6d6 at 18th level.<br />\n<strong>Transmute Self.</strong> As a reaction, you can spend cursed energy to transmute yourself in one of the following ways (X = CE modifier):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Harden (2 CE)</strong> You harden your body and gain a +4 bonus to AC until the start of your turn.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Shell (X CE)</strong> You create a shell over your body and gain 5 temporary hit points per cursed energy spent.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Slick (2 CE)</strong> You cover parts of your body in a solution and gain a 20 ft bonus to walking speed and do not provoke opportunity attacks until the start of your turn.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
